\section{Introduction}
Fuliiru (Kifuliiru, flr) is a Bantu language of South Kivu province, Democratic Republic of the Congo. Estimates of speakers vary; one 1999 estimate gives 300,000. Search results turned up Scripture and religious media but no dictionary, primer or school material.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found. No literacy programmes, primers or textbooks appeared in search results.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Overview of the Fuliru people: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuliru_people}
\end{itemize}
No dictionary or grammar was found.

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Kifuliiru Bible (\emph{Ibibiriya}), eBible.org, (c) 2018 Wycliffe Bible Translators: \url{https://ebible.org/study/content/texts/flr/about.html}
\item Scripture Earth resources for Fuliiru: \url{https://www.scriptureearth.org/00eng.php?iso=flr}
\item Joshua Project language page: \url{https://www.joshuaproject.net/index.php/languages/flr}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Global Recordings Network audio recordings: \url{https://www.globalrecordings.net/en/language/flr}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
The complete Bible text gives a corpus of written Fuliiru, usable for building reading materials. Basic educational resources are missing: orthography documentation, a dictionary, graded readers and teacher guides would all have to be produced. The language is not known to be taught in schools.

\end{document}
